# Tosca Cloud AI Agent Skills (hybrid CLI)

Always-on baseline for coding agents driving **Tricentis Tosca Cloud**. **Default:** **`toscactl`**. **Gaps:** **`tn`**. Read **`tosca-cloud-basics`** first.

**Prerequisite:** `toscactl login`; `python3 verify_toscactl.py`. Gap workflows: `configure_tn_connection.py` + `tn --setup`.

## Which skill

| Task | Skill |
|---|---|
| Connect | `tosca-cloud-connect` |
| Basics | `tosca-cloud-basics` |
| Analyze latest run | `tosca-analyzing-execution-results` |
| Execution history | `tosca-analyzing-execution-history` |
| Remediate | `tosca-remediating-from-results` |
| Author manual TC | `tosca-authoring-manual-testcase` |
| Author automated TC | `tosca-authoring-automated-testcase` |
| Explain TC | `tosca-explaining-testcase` |
| Orchestration | `tosca-cloud` |

## Guardrails

1. Read-only unless asked.
2. Use `runtime-routing.md` — toscactl default, tn for gaps.
3. Never echo secrets.
4. Delegate to `toscactl` or `tn` in terminal.
5. Search before mutate.

Install **one** Cloud automation path per IDE profile — not both.
